    "shop_smart":  [
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eBuy the roast on sale.\u003c/strong\u003e Chuck roast goes on markdown all the time. When you see a good price, grab it and freeze it. This whole batch is built around one cheap cut stretched across fourteen meals.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eOne little can of chipotles goes a long way.\u003c/strong\u003e Chipotles in adobo are cheap and last. Freeze the leftover peppers in a small bag so nothing goes to waste and the next batch costs even less.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eDry rice and canned beans keep it cheap.\u003c/strong\u003e Cooking rice yourself costs pennies per serving. If you are short on time, store brand canned beans keep the price low without any fuss."
